cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or reference this software, please cite it as below."
authors:
  - family-names: "Whittaker"
    given-names: "Timothy"
    email: "tdw419@gmail.com"
title: "Visual Audio & Geometry OS: Spatial Computing, Bootable Pixel Substrates, and the Glyph Architecture"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-09"
url: "https://github.com/tdw419/visual_audio"
repository-code: "https://github.com/tdw419/visual_audio"
abstract: >-
  Geometry OS and the Visual Audio system represent a paradigm shift from symbolic
  to spatial computing. It implements "The Screen is the Hard Drive" and "The Screen
  is the Mind" through Hilbert-curve packed 2D pixel containers (VAC2/PXC1/.rts.png)
  bootable directly via hypervisor block backends (virtio_pixel_backend), executed
  by a dual-substrate spatial ISA (Glyph ISA v2 with lockstep CPU and WGSL GPU twins),
  and self-hosted through machine-proven in-image tile admission.
keywords:
  - "spatial computing"
  - "geometry os"
  - "pixel os"
  - "glyph isa"
  - "hilbert curve"
  - "virtio-blk"
  - "formal verification"
  - "self-hosting"
